    "probe_text": "POST `/api/owners` is handled by `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:212`). Here is everything that happens, in execution order.\n\n## 0. Boundary (before the method body)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n- **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`), the standard JSR-380 pass:\n  - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n  - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n  - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n  - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n  - `title` `@Size(max 10)`; `address` `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1` `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2` `@Size(max 255)`; `email` `@Size(max 255)`\n  - `sharesHousehold` defaults to `false` when omitted.\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n1. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (trimmed; blank/absent \u2192 ignored). If that key was already recorded *and* the owner it created still exists, returns that existing owner with **200 OK** and does nothing further. (`idempotencyKey()` / `idempotentCreates`.)\n\n2. **`normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect on the DTO)* \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands whole-token street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) for `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address`; writes back the canonical lines and the **composed** `address` (structured lines preferred over the flat field). Runs before the required-field check so a fully-blank address is treated as missing.\n\n3. **`validateRequiredFields`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 rejects if `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank (whitespace-only counts). All offending field names are collected into the `errors` array (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n4. **`normalizeTelephone` \u2192 `toE164`** *(validation \u2192 400 + side-effect)* \u2014 converts to E.164: keeps a leading `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets. Must be 8\u201315 digits after `+`; for known country codes the national length must match exactly (`+1`\u219210, `+61`\u21929). Valid result written back onto the DTO. Invalid \u2192 400 naming `telephone`.\n\n5. **`normalizeEmail`** *(validation \u2192 400 + side-effect)* \u2014 `email` is optional; if present it must match the email regex, and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Trimmed + lower-cased value written back. Invalid/disposable \u2192 400 naming `email`.\n\n6. **`validatePostcode`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 `postcode` optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits and, for a city that derives to a known region, fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit value. Invalid \u2192 400 naming `postcode`.\n\n7. **`computeHouseholdId`** *(derivation)* \u2014 first 12 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 of `\"<normalizedLastName>|<postcode>\"`; `null` when no postcode.\n\n8. **`rejectDuplicate`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true` (which bypasses the whole block), scans existing owners (skipping soft-deleted ones) and rejects if the new owner matches an existing `householdId`, or matches the derived `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`). Conflict \u2192 409 naming `identityKey`.\n\n9. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 409 naming `city`.\n\n10. **`resolveRegistrationDate`** *(validation \u2192 400 + side-effect)* \u2014 defaults to server's current date when omitted; a supplied future date \u2192 400 naming `registrationDate`; the effective date is rolled forward off weekends and listed public holidays to the next business day, and written back onto the DTO.\n\n11. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** *(validation \u2192 429)* \u2014 counts existing owners already carrying that resolved `registrationDate`; if \u2265 100 (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 429 (`DailyOwnerLimitReachedException`).\n\nThen the entity is built and derived fields are assigned (side-effects on the new `Owner`):\n\n12. **`ownerMapper.toOwner`** \u2014 map DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`id`, `pets`, `customerCode` ignored).\n13. **`setHouseholdId`** \u2014 from step 7.\n14. **`assignCustomerCode`** \u2014 `\"<REGION>-<HASH8>\"` (region from postcode, else city; HASH8 = SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName`), then de-duplicated against existing codes with a `-<n>` suffix.\n15. **`assignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 `\"<customerCode>-M<YY>\"`, `YY` = last two digits of the registration date's fiscal year.\n16. **`assignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners sharing `firstName`+`lastName` (case-insensitive).\n17. **`assignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 `true` when > 80 existing owners already carry that registration date.\n18. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (lowest matching id) when an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone.\n19. **`assignHouseholdMembership`** \u2014 `householdMemberCount` = new owner + existing owners sharing the `householdId` (null when no household).\n20. **`assignMembership`** \u2014 computes `membershipPoints` (+2 email present, +1 namesakeCount==0, +2 household \u22653, +3 tenure \u2014 always 0 on create) and maps to `membershipLevel` (1/2/3/4).\n\nFinally:\n\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persists the new owner.\n22. **Idempotency record** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` for future repeats.\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` info line with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`.\n24. **Response** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (with its many derived read fields), sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, returns **201 Created**.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the doc comment on `assignMembership` (and the constant `TENURE_LEVEL_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS`) says tenure never contributes on create because `tenureFiscalYears` is hard-coded to return `0` \u2014 so the +3 tenure branch (step 20) is dead on this path, capping a newly created owner at level 3."
